# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FayTarra environment
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Browsing works with NO configuration: with no Supabase keys set the app uses
# the bundled local JSON driver (./.data/faytarra.json), auto-seeded with a
# realistic sample community.
#
# ACCOUNTS NEED SUPABASE. Sign-up and sign-in are Supabase Auth — FayTarra
# never hashes, stores or checks a password. Without the two NEXT_PUBLIC_ keys
# below the auth screens say accounts are switched off; there is deliberately
# no local fallback login.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Supabase Auth (required for accounts) ---------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# The absolute URL Supabase puts in confirmation and password-reset emails.
# On Vercel this falls back to the deployment URL, which is right for previews
# and wrong for a custom domain. Add <this>/auth/callback to the redirect
# allow-list in Supabase → Authentication → URL configuration.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-domain

# --- Supabase database + storage -------------------------------------------
# Server-side only. Also used to delete an account's Supabase Auth user.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key

# Storage bucket used for uploaded images/video when Supabase is configured.
# SUPABASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=faytarra-media

# --- Local development ------------------------------------------------------
# Where the local JSON driver stores data. Defaults to ./.data at the project
# root. Only used when Supabase is not configured.
# FAYTARRA_DATA_DIR=/var/lib/faytarra

# Show the seeded demo credentials on the sign-in page. Only meaningful after
# `npm run seed` has created those accounts in Supabase Auth.
# FAYTARRA_SHOW_DEMO_LOGIN=1

# Comma separated list of emails that are granted the admin role on signup.
# ADMIN_EMAILS=you@example.com
